1
00:00:15,339 --> 00:00:17,422
HA JUNG-WOO

2
00:00:17,423 --> 00:00:19,423
IM SOO-JUNG

3
00:00:22,793 --> 00:00:25,023
KIM JUN-HAN

4
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:27,317
KRYSTAL JUNG

5
00:00:33,805 --> 00:00:35,602
SHIM EUN-KYUNG

6
00:00:54,505 --> 00:00:58,938
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

7
00:00:59,938 --> 00:01:03,738
FIVE YEARS AGO, ONE DAY

8
00:01:10,471 --> 00:01:11,371
It's nice, right?

9
00:01:11,871 --> 00:01:12,805
It's nice.

10
00:01:18,505 --> 00:01:20,072
Oh my! Yi-gyeong!

11
00:01:20,818 --> 00:01:23,039
Help!

12
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:24,705
Yi-gyeong, are you okay? Oh my!

13
00:01:25,805 --> 00:01:26,905
Oh my, Yi-gyeong!

14
00:01:27,872 --> 00:01:28,405
What's going on?

15
00:01:29,739 --> 00:01:31,038
Help us!

16
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:32,072
What's going on?

17
00:01:32,339 --> 00:01:33,472
Help us!

18
00:01:34,439 --> 00:01:35,105
Seon!

19
00:01:36,005 --> 00:01:36,872
What's wrong?

20
00:01:38,339 --> 00:01:39,272
Whoa!

21
00:01:40,672 --> 00:01:42,505
Jeez, that punk.

22
00:01:45,405 --> 00:01:47,839
- You crazy bastard! Gosh!
- You scared me!

23
00:01:51,799 --> 00:01:54,076
Hey, don't mess around here.

24
00:01:54,671 --> 00:01:57,504
Are you crazy?
Why are you joking around at this place?

25
00:01:57,505 --> 00:01:59,872
You're so immature, Min Hwal-sung.

26
00:02:00,672 --> 00:02:03,404
Why are you acting like that? Huh?

27
00:02:03,405 --> 00:02:05,638
I told you
not to joke around here.

28
00:02:11,139 --> 00:02:12,439
Seriously.

29
00:02:16,452 --> 00:02:18,518
If your wife falls
in the water, would you save her?

30
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:20,938
Hey, didn't you see me
jump into the water earlier?

31
00:02:22,030 --> 00:02:24,030
- The weather's really nice.
- Yeah.

32
00:02:27,872 --> 00:02:29,572
What are those two talking about?

33
00:02:29,684 --> 00:02:30,841
I'm not saving her.

34
00:02:31,339 --> 00:02:32,239
Why not?

35
00:02:33,372 --> 00:02:35,372
Do you know
how much Yi-gyeong is worth?

36
00:02:37,718 --> 00:02:40,118
Hey, you seem
kind of serious about this.

37
00:02:43,305 --> 00:02:45,239
I'm just kidding, man.

38
00:02:49,105 --> 00:02:50,005
Yes.

39
00:03:05,339 --> 00:03:07,538
Come on in!

40
00:03:07,539 --> 00:03:08,771
Hurry in!

41
00:03:08,772 --> 00:03:09,772
Alright.

42
00:03:16,839 --> 00:03:25,572
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

43
00:03:27,472 --> 00:03:28,638
- Grab him!
- Get him!

44
00:03:28,639 --> 00:03:30,439
EPISODE 3
Damn it!

45
00:03:40,072 --> 00:03:40,772
Open the door!

46
00:03:59,705 --> 00:04:00,672
Damn!

47
00:04:44,305 --> 00:04:44,672
Ah!

48
00:04:46,905 --> 00:04:48,472
Oh!

49
00:04:52,905 --> 00:04:53,772
Jeez!

50
00:05:04,405 --> 00:05:05,405
Sergeant.

51
00:05:05,925 --> 00:05:06,658
What's going on?

52
00:05:07,072 --> 00:05:08,605
What happened?

53
00:05:08,772 --> 00:05:09,639
What about the culprit?

54
00:05:12,045 --> 00:05:12,948
Did you lose him?

55
00:05:27,072 --> 00:05:28,571
Damn.

56
00:05:28,572 --> 00:05:29,504
Hurry down and check!

57
00:05:29,505 --> 00:05:30,572
- Yes, sir!
- Yes!

58
00:05:52,405 --> 00:05:53,305
Hwal-sung.

59
00:06:18,039 --> 00:06:19,004
He's still alive.

60
00:06:19,005 --> 00:06:20,539
I'm at Bugwang Skyroad
in the parking lot.

61
00:06:34,539 --> 00:06:37,239
Please help me!

62
00:07:23,805 --> 00:07:25,005
What's going on?

63
00:07:25,472 --> 00:07:26,504
Um...

64
00:07:26,505 --> 00:07:27,639
Are you okay?

65
00:07:28,039 --> 00:07:29,572
My car is out of gas.

66
00:07:31,972 --> 00:07:33,305
Did you call
your insurance company?

67
00:07:34,685 --> 00:07:36,818
Well, my phone's dead right now.

68
00:07:37,472 --> 00:07:38,705
Hold on a second.

69
00:07:41,318 --> 00:07:43,471
Looking here,
there's a gas station nearby.

70
00:07:43,472 --> 00:07:45,900
I'll go get some gas for you.

71
00:07:45,901 --> 00:07:47,138
No, that's okay.

72
00:07:47,139 --> 00:07:48,471
No, I insist.
We should help each other.

73
00:07:48,472 --> 00:07:50,304
- You really don't have to.
- It's raining too.

74
00:07:50,305 --> 00:07:52,572
Please sit in the car. I'll be right back.

75
00:08:24,239 --> 00:08:25,572
Gosh.

76
00:08:29,005 --> 00:08:29,972
What's this?

77
00:08:31,539 --> 00:08:32,839
Where did he go?

78
00:08:35,239 --> 00:08:36,205
Did he just leave his car?

79
00:08:51,139 --> 00:08:53,439
Can't I just
sleep a bit at home?

80
00:08:54,147 --> 00:08:55,872
The sergeant told us to wait.

81
00:08:59,453 --> 00:09:01,520
I should go
to the sauna and wash up.

82
00:09:03,525 --> 00:09:05,825
- I'm going crazy here!
- Oh, you're here?

83
00:09:08,105 --> 00:09:08,871
Hey!

84
00:09:08,872 --> 00:09:10,105
Are you praying or something?

85
00:09:11,872 --> 00:09:15,071
Hey, Ms. Jeon met with the chief himself.

86
00:09:15,072 --> 00:09:17,942
If we can't find the daughter,
we're done for.

87
00:09:18,398 --> 00:09:19,931
We just need to catch the culprit.

88
00:09:20,605 --> 00:09:22,839
I mean, the punk slipped away
right in front of us!

89
00:09:23,972 --> 00:09:24,839
Jeez.

90
00:09:28,239 --> 00:09:29,869
Yongdaemun Police,
Violent Crimes Division speaking.

91
00:09:31,839 --> 00:09:32,772
What?

92
00:09:34,872 --> 00:09:35,938
They're saying they found the daughter.

93
00:09:35,939 --> 00:09:37,052
What?

94
00:09:37,239 --> 00:09:37,905
Where?

95
00:09:38,339 --> 00:09:39,605
In Mungyang, Gyeonggi-do.

96
00:09:40,172 --> 00:09:41,804
Hey, hey! Let's go!

97
00:09:41,805 --> 00:09:43,638
Hurry up! Let's get moving!

98
00:09:43,639 --> 00:09:45,471
Yes, thank you.
We're on our way right now.

99
00:09:45,472 --> 00:09:46,439
Hurry up!

100
00:09:48,105 --> 00:09:49,105
Goodness!

101
00:09:54,805 --> 00:09:56,505
She was left like this...

102
00:10:06,239 --> 00:10:06,939
AMBULANCE

103
00:12:01,939 --> 00:12:03,872
KIDNAPPING

104
00:12:04,739 --> 00:12:05,472
Cases of minors being lured
via social media are increasing

105
00:12:14,472 --> 00:12:16,372
ABDUCTION

106
00:12:49,405 --> 00:12:51,305
Remove all videos from the screen?
Confirm

107
00:13:26,105 --> 00:13:28,139
Jeez.

108
00:13:29,838 --> 00:13:31,738
How long do you plan
to keep getting disrespected?

109
00:13:34,837 --> 00:13:36,037
Seventy million.

110
00:13:37,139 --> 00:13:38,739
Nine hundred eighty million.

111
00:13:39,772 --> 00:13:40,805
Nine hundred ninety million.

112
00:13:44,172 --> 00:13:47,805
I said I'd pay it back, you punks.

113
00:13:56,639 --> 00:13:59,505
ONE BILLION

114
00:14:26,978 --> 00:14:29,178
What are you doing at this hour?

115
00:14:31,072 --> 00:14:33,639
I couldn't fall sleep...

116
00:14:37,105 --> 00:14:40,905
Dad didn't come home yesterday, right?

117
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,272
Is something wrong?

118
00:14:44,572 --> 00:14:45,572
Oh,

119
00:14:46,072 --> 00:14:47,372
he said he had some things to do.

120
00:14:47,805 --> 00:14:49,872
What things?

121
00:14:52,839 --> 00:14:55,338
Did you take your vitamins yesterday?

122
00:15:00,405 --> 00:15:01,736
You didn't take them.

123
00:15:02,405 --> 00:15:05,006
I told you so many times
to take them.

124
00:15:05,718 --> 00:15:07,318
Do I have to spoon-feed you?

125
00:15:08,005 --> 00:15:10,823
If you go to America,
you won't be able to keep your energy up.

126
00:15:11,939 --> 00:15:15,705
Gosh. It's dawn and you're nagging me...

127
00:15:16,438 --> 00:15:18,504
Do I say this for my own sake?

128
00:15:18,505 --> 00:15:19,805
- It's all for your own good...
- Really?

129
00:15:20,505 --> 00:15:24,205
To me, it sounds like you want me
to go abroad for your benefit.

130
00:15:24,705 --> 00:15:25,639
What?

131
00:15:27,805 --> 00:15:29,205
What's with her?

132
00:15:39,472 --> 00:15:41,839
JEON YI-GYEONG

133
00:15:50,239 --> 00:15:51,567
Hello?

134
00:15:51,568 --> 00:15:53,113
Is this Kim Seon?

135
00:15:54,032 --> 00:15:55,693
Yes, who is this?

136
00:15:56,605 --> 00:15:57,872
This is Yi-gyeong's number.

137
00:15:58,339 --> 00:15:59,772
This is the hospital.

138
00:16:00,357 --> 00:16:03,097
I'm Detective Koh Ju-ran
from Yongdaemun Precinct.

139
00:16:04,272 --> 00:16:07,071
I'm calling because Ms. Jeon Yi-gyeong
says she can only ask

140
00:16:07,072 --> 00:16:08,605
Ms. Kim Seon for help.

141
00:16:09,466 --> 00:16:10,972
Yes, I see.

142
00:16:47,472 --> 00:16:48,372
Who's there?

143
00:16:49,039 --> 00:16:50,005
It's me.

144
00:16:52,172 --> 00:16:53,239
Hey, open the door.

145
00:16:56,305 --> 00:16:57,271
Hey.

146
00:16:57,272 --> 00:16:58,239
What happened to you?

147
00:17:04,872 --> 00:17:06,372
Were you planning to keep all that money?

148
00:17:08,732 --> 00:17:10,065
What do you mean by that?

149
00:17:10,679 --> 00:17:12,212
You think you can get away?

150
00:17:14,005 --> 00:17:15,139
Gi Su-jong.

151
00:17:16,445 --> 00:17:17,945
Do you really think you can?

152
00:17:19,118 --> 00:17:20,018
What?

153
00:17:23,405 --> 00:17:24,471
Gi Su-jong,

154
00:17:24,472 --> 00:17:27,072
you are under arrest for robbery,
assault, and kidnapping.

155
00:17:27,705 --> 00:17:28,672
Get on your knees!

156
00:17:29,959 --> 00:17:31,335
Wait...

157
00:17:31,639 --> 00:17:32,239
What?

158
00:17:33,439 --> 00:17:34,638
Just a moment!

159
00:17:34,639 --> 00:17:37,238
Please let me pay back my money
and my building debt.

160
00:17:37,239 --> 00:17:37,939
Please?

161
00:17:38,072 --> 00:17:38,639
Wait!

162
00:17:44,239 --> 00:17:45,039
Huh?

163
00:17:58,072 --> 00:17:59,205
Honey...

164
00:17:59,972 --> 00:18:01,604
Let go! Let me go!

165
00:18:01,605 --> 00:18:04,205
Let go!

166
00:18:05,505 --> 00:18:07,039
Let go of me!

167
00:18:08,072 --> 00:18:09,172
No!

168
00:18:42,398 --> 00:18:44,132
To my beloved wife Seon,

169
00:18:44,918 --> 00:18:46,818
if you receive this letter,

170
00:18:46,819 --> 00:18:49,019
the worst scenario I can imagine
has become a reality.

171
00:18:53,018 --> 00:18:53,851
Hello?

172
00:18:54,805 --> 00:18:56,205
Isn't your cell phone working?

173
00:18:57,324 --> 00:18:58,324
Oh...

174
00:18:58,325 --> 00:18:59,538
Well, it's just that...

175
00:18:59,539 --> 00:19:02,135
My phone is broken.
The screen got cracked.

176
00:19:02,136 --> 00:19:03,569
Hurry to
Korean University Hospital.

177
00:19:04,905 --> 00:19:05,772
Why?

178
00:19:06,105 --> 00:19:08,039
A detective contacted me.

179
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:10,155
Hwal-sung and Yi-gyeong
are both in the hospital.

180
00:19:10,845 --> 00:19:12,512
Hwal-sung is unconscious.

181
00:19:13,025 --> 00:19:15,592
I'm going to pack Yi-gyeong's
things and head to the hospital.

182
00:19:15,593 --> 00:19:16,726
You should come quickly too.

183
00:19:19,226 --> 00:19:20,559
Are you listening to me?

184
00:19:20,872 --> 00:19:22,139
Honey, but

185
00:19:22,924 --> 00:19:24,624
I've got to be somewhere

186
00:19:24,625 --> 00:19:26,459
when the sun comes up. So I was wondering

187
00:19:26,683 --> 00:19:28,071
if I could I go during the afternoon?

188
00:19:28,072 --> 00:19:28,972
What?

189
00:19:29,272 --> 00:19:30,639
Are you out of your mind?

190
00:19:31,225 --> 00:19:33,492
Your best friend is in a vegetative state.

191
00:19:33,493 --> 00:19:34,493
Where are you going?

192
00:19:36,623 --> 00:19:38,356
Get yourself together
and listen to me.

193
00:19:39,077 --> 00:19:41,577
Come to the hospital and make a visit.
Understand?

194
00:19:42,789 --> 00:19:44,189
Yes, I understand.

195
00:20:01,223 --> 00:20:02,523
Gosh.

196
00:20:02,923 --> 00:20:04,122
Mr. Gi.

197
00:20:04,123 --> 00:20:05,855
Someone shattered all the flower pots.

198
00:20:05,856 --> 00:20:07,222
This is ridiculous.

199
00:20:07,223 --> 00:20:08,422
Let's check the CCTV, okay?

200
00:20:08,423 --> 00:20:09,990
I need to file a police report.

201
00:20:10,469 --> 00:20:11,736
Wow.

202
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:13,555
Okay.

203
00:20:13,556 --> 00:20:15,255
But I really have to go right now.

204
00:20:15,256 --> 00:20:16,689
- I'll see you later.
- Wait.

205
00:20:16,690 --> 00:20:18,474
By the outfit,
it's obvious you're going hiking.

206
00:20:18,475 --> 00:20:20,039
Stop in and let's talk for a moment.

207
00:20:20,323 --> 00:20:22,222
- Sorry, Dong-ki.
- But.

208
00:20:22,223 --> 00:20:24,423
But, wait.

209
00:20:25,456 --> 00:20:26,790
That guy...

210
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:50,556
Sent by: Lee Morgan
Kidnapping at Pyeong-buk Gwan last night

211
00:20:50,557 --> 00:20:51,110
The son-in-law fell into a coma while
trying to exchange with the kidnapper

212
00:20:51,111 --> 00:20:51,692
The daughter was found by police
in a weakened state

213
00:20:51,693 --> 00:20:52,305
Three billion won and the whereabouts
of the kidnapper are still unknown

214
00:21:03,056 --> 00:21:04,190
I came to pay off my debt.

215
00:21:05,756 --> 00:21:08,090
Did you set up a meeting?

216
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:10,256
What meeting?

217
00:21:11,123 --> 00:21:12,922
It's still before business hours.

218
00:21:12,923 --> 00:21:15,123
There's no such thing.
I said I came to pay off my debt.

219
00:21:15,390 --> 00:21:16,690
You don't know me?
The Seyoon Building guy.

220
00:21:17,123 --> 00:21:18,055
Yes.

221
00:21:18,056 --> 00:21:19,523
Gi Su-jong,

222
00:21:19,524 --> 00:21:20,957
sir...

223
00:21:24,490 --> 00:21:26,256
We starts at 10 AM.

224
00:21:28,156 --> 00:21:29,927
I don't know about that.

225
00:21:30,223 --> 00:21:33,024
You should have
texted me in advance then.

226
00:21:33,978 --> 00:21:36,089
Try counting after 10 AM then.

227
00:21:36,090 --> 00:21:39,122
This isn't a personal deal.

228
00:21:39,123 --> 00:21:40,422
We have to follow procedures.

229
00:21:41,209 --> 00:21:42,376
Procedures are good.

230
00:21:46,628 --> 00:21:48,722
I have to go,

231
00:21:48,723 --> 00:21:50,090
- so I'll head out first.
- But,

232
00:21:55,190 --> 00:21:56,005
wait a second.

233
00:21:59,056 --> 00:22:00,056
Wait.

234
00:22:05,590 --> 00:22:06,567
My brother-in-law.

235
00:22:07,530 --> 00:22:08,663
It was you guys, right?

236
00:22:11,329 --> 00:22:12,496
Oh.

237
00:22:14,049 --> 00:22:15,582
Rest in peace.

238
00:22:16,523 --> 00:22:17,422
What?

239
00:22:17,423 --> 00:22:20,390
What is that in Korean?

240
00:22:21,223 --> 00:22:22,522
To the deceased,

241
00:22:22,523 --> 00:22:23,822
- May you rest,
- may you rest,

242
00:22:23,823 --> 00:22:24,990
- peacefully.
- peacefully.

243
00:22:25,656 --> 00:22:26,423
Right?

244
00:22:30,023 --> 00:22:31,184
Seriously.

245
00:22:31,923 --> 00:22:33,156
- Look here.
- Yes?

246
00:22:33,890 --> 00:22:35,023
Hey, move aside.

247
00:22:41,730 --> 00:22:43,130
Come after 10 AM.

248
00:23:16,290 --> 00:23:17,323
It's nice.

249
00:23:31,090 --> 00:23:32,190
A bag...

250
00:23:38,423 --> 00:23:40,656
She said there's underwear
and socks in here.

251
00:24:06,423 --> 00:24:07,555
SIX WEEKS / THE DAY I FIRST MET YOU

252
00:24:07,556 --> 00:24:09,690
Next, I'll hear your heartbeat
Thank you for coming to Mom and Dad

253
00:24:14,123 --> 00:24:14,989
Eight weeks
The day I heard your strong heartbeat!

254
00:24:14,990 --> 00:24:15,989
I WAS SO MOVED, I ALMOST CRIED

255
00:24:15,990 --> 00:24:16,923
IT'S A SECRET THAT DAD CRIED A LOT

256
00:24:19,890 --> 00:24:21,822
You have Da-rae, don't you?

257
00:24:21,823 --> 00:24:23,156
That's what I envy the most.

258
00:25:01,304 --> 00:25:01,956
MESSAGE

259
00:25:12,656 --> 00:25:15,923
SU-JONG: IS IT REALLY SAFE?

260
00:25:21,908 --> 00:25:24,227
I investigated
the suspect's vehicle.

261
00:25:24,423 --> 00:25:25,522
And

262
00:25:25,523 --> 00:25:28,150
it's a rental car, so it's a bit unclear.

263
00:25:28,770 --> 00:25:29,770
So what is it?

264
00:25:31,023 --> 00:25:33,516
The previous owner was Jung Chang-su.

265
00:25:33,890 --> 00:25:35,255
Jung Chang-su?

266
00:25:35,256 --> 00:25:36,828
That missing construction company CEO?

267
00:25:37,123 --> 00:25:37,956
Yes.

268
00:25:40,236 --> 00:25:41,702
Okay then. Please send the address.

269
00:25:42,390 --> 00:25:45,023
Yes, right away.

270
00:26:00,556 --> 00:26:02,956
CHANG-SU CONSTRUCTION & DEVELOPMENT

271
00:26:21,323 --> 00:26:24,090
CEO JUNG CHANG-SU

272
00:27:23,556 --> 00:27:25,322
MIN HWAL-SUNG

273
00:27:25,323 --> 00:27:27,156
CHANG-SU CONSTRUCTION CEO JUNG CHANG-SU

274
00:27:27,490 --> 00:27:28,823
Min Hwal-sung.

275
00:27:35,690 --> 00:27:36,423
Sejeong-ro Urban Renewal
Redevelopment Zone 3 Maintenance Plan

