00:43:53,556 --> 00:43:55,023
Yes, sure.

557
00:43:55,790 --> 00:43:56,956
That's not it.

558
00:43:57,323 --> 00:43:58,356
NAME: WI SEO-HUN

559
00:43:59,023 --> 00:44:00,855
Hmm, that person

560
00:44:00,856 --> 00:44:03,890
didn't looked like a criminal.

561
00:44:06,523 --> 00:44:07,790
Then by any chance...

562
00:44:09,790 --> 00:44:11,723
- Is this the person?
- Excuse me?

563
00:44:11,990 --> 00:44:13,556
The person from last night

564
00:44:13,557 --> 00:44:14,826
who escaped after leaving his car,

565
00:44:15,190 --> 00:44:16,323
is he the one?

566
00:44:22,056 --> 00:44:23,889
Well, I've only seen

567
00:44:23,890 --> 00:44:25,523
the masked side of him.

568
00:44:26,223 --> 00:44:28,090
CAPTAIN TOAST

569
00:44:36,056 --> 00:44:36,955
Yes?

570
00:44:36,956 --> 00:44:40,823
Why did you
buy toast when we're having beef?

571
00:44:41,223 --> 00:44:42,123
Oh, this?

572
00:44:43,023 --> 00:44:44,023
They say this place is good.

573
00:44:45,423 --> 00:44:46,290
You can eat it later.

574
00:44:46,990 --> 00:44:49,723
First, let's eat the meat, Da-rae.

575
00:44:55,490 --> 00:44:56,523
Oh, and

576
00:44:58,090 --> 00:44:58,956
here.

577
00:45:01,823 --> 00:45:05,256
Surgical guide for cochlear implant /
Device for severe hearing loss

578
00:45:11,856 --> 00:45:12,823
Dad...

579
00:45:13,122 --> 00:45:14,522
Da-rae.

580
00:45:16,190 --> 00:45:18,871
Let's go to America and get the surgery.

581
00:45:19,490 --> 00:45:20,623
I'll book everything.

582
00:45:23,056 --> 00:45:26,889
But the insurance
won't cover this and it's very expensive.

583
00:45:26,890 --> 00:45:27,790
Oh.

584
00:45:28,090 --> 00:45:29,290
Don't worry.

585
00:45:30,090 --> 00:45:31,856
Your dad is a landlord.

586
00:45:41,890 --> 00:45:44,756
I don't need
the surgery.

587
00:45:45,817 --> 00:45:47,450
Come on, what are you saying?

588
00:45:48,323 --> 00:45:49,671
You have to get it.

589
00:45:53,328 --> 00:45:54,302
Eat, Da-rae.

590
00:46:03,689 --> 00:46:05,422
Captain Kang,
please go to his home.

591
00:46:05,423 --> 00:46:06,589
Okay.
Detective Baek, follow me this way.

592
00:46:06,590 --> 00:46:07,756
- Bo-ram.
- Yes.

593
00:46:14,323 --> 00:46:16,955
I don't have to tell the sergeant, right?

594
00:46:16,956 --> 00:46:18,423
I'll handle it.

595
00:46:27,990 --> 00:46:32,290
If I have surgery,
can I listen to music?

596
00:46:32,657 --> 00:46:33,832
Oh, of course.

597
00:46:34,890 --> 00:46:35,923
What do you want to listen to?

598
00:46:38,256 --> 00:46:39,990
Well...

599
00:46:40,923 --> 00:46:42,023
Hmm...

600
00:46:42,656 --> 00:46:44,390
BTS?

601
00:46:46,223 --> 00:46:47,589
Blackpink?

602
00:46:48,323 --> 00:46:49,222
Panic?

603
00:46:49,223 --> 00:46:51,855
That's what we listen to.

604
00:46:51,856 --> 00:46:52,456
Really?

605
00:46:54,456 --> 00:46:57,255
I'm fine
with anything.

606
00:46:57,256 --> 00:47:02,031
I want to hear the song
my mom and dad sing.

607
00:47:09,323 --> 00:47:15,722
Just something like when you're whistling.

608
00:47:15,723 --> 00:47:19,290
I want to hear you snore too...

609
00:47:33,956 --> 00:47:34,855
Oh.

610
00:47:34,856 --> 00:47:36,455
Seeing the family all together,

611
00:47:36,456 --> 00:47:37,723
it seems like something good happened.

612
00:47:44,823 --> 00:47:45,864
What's going on?

613
00:47:56,190 --> 00:47:58,190
- Aren't you going to ask?
- Ask what?

614
00:47:59,323 --> 00:48:00,990
You're not asking why we're taking you.

615
00:48:01,956 --> 00:48:02,813
Oh.

616
00:48:03,413 --> 00:48:04,655
Why am I being taken?

617
00:48:04,656 --> 00:48:05,856
You'll find out
when we get there.

618
00:48:09,616 --> 00:48:11,755
Oh, I knew this would happen.

619
00:48:11,756 --> 00:48:14,190
That guy gives me the creeps every time.

620
00:48:49,490 --> 00:48:52,090
Hearing impaired,
examination, surgery guide

621
00:49:26,156 --> 00:49:27,537
I've been strange lately,
haven't I?

622
00:49:28,523 --> 00:49:31,310
And you're probably resenting me a lot.

623
00:49:31,890 --> 00:49:34,855
Even if the world blames me,

624
00:49:34,856 --> 00:49:37,471
I hope you and Da-rae

625
00:49:38,342 --> 00:49:40,003
will believe in me.

626
00:49:57,189 --> 00:49:59,056
I heard the building has a lot of debt.

627
00:49:59,390 --> 00:50:01,269
Who in Korea buys a building

628
00:50:01,270 --> 00:50:02,370
with their own money?

629
00:50:03,290 --> 00:50:04,390
You go into debt to buy it.

630
00:50:04,990 --> 00:50:08,223
It seems like you were trying
to scramble for cash?

631
00:50:09,556 --> 00:50:11,345
Who told you that?

632
00:50:11,923 --> 00:50:13,567
Who said it is not important.

633
00:50:14,023 --> 00:50:15,689
You just need

634
00:50:15,690 --> 00:50:16,823
to tell us the facts.

635
00:50:17,123 --> 00:50:19,223
Yes, I have no debt.

636
00:50:20,623 --> 00:50:21,855
None?

637
00:50:21,856 --> 00:50:22,689
None.

638
00:50:22,690 --> 00:50:23,690
How so?

639
00:50:26,156 --> 00:50:29,389
To be precise, I'm in a situation
where I'm paying off my debt.

640
00:50:29,390 --> 00:50:30,408
So?

641
00:50:31,023 --> 00:50:33,223
How are you paying it off?

642
00:50:33,669 --> 00:50:35,136
It can't be just a little bit.

643
00:50:35,589 --> 00:50:38,190
I'm working part-time and paying it off.

644
00:50:38,890 --> 00:50:42,756
But do I really need to share
personal stuff like this?

645
00:50:47,422 --> 00:50:49,755
Then on the night of the kidnapping
with Min Hwal-sung and Jeon Yi-gyeong,

646
00:50:49,756 --> 00:50:50,656
where were you?

647
00:50:51,023 --> 00:50:51,923
I was at home.

648
00:50:52,743 --> 00:50:54,099
Do you have anyone who can testify?

649
00:50:54,913 --> 00:50:58,956
Before going home,
I think I was at the Seyoon Building.

650
00:51:00,942 --> 00:51:01,909
So I'm asking

651
00:51:02,290 --> 00:51:03,855
where were you

652
00:51:03,856 --> 00:51:04,656
yesterday?

653
00:51:05,590 --> 00:51:06,490
At home.

654
00:51:08,022 --> 00:51:09,381
Who can testify?

655
00:51:09,956 --> 00:51:11,790
My daughter and my wife.

656
00:51:14,490 --> 00:51:15,755
I mean,

657
00:51:15,756 --> 00:51:19,156
is a witness even needed here?

658
00:51:19,656 --> 00:51:20,590
Mr. Gi Su-jong,

659
00:51:21,790 --> 00:51:24,122
if you come clean now,

660
00:51:24,123 --> 00:51:25,223
it could be taken into account.

661
00:51:25,690 --> 00:51:27,489
Excuse me, I really don't get

662
00:51:27,490 --> 00:51:29,223
what this situation is.

663
00:51:32,150 --> 00:51:33,583
- Just a moment.
- Sure.

664
00:51:41,356 --> 00:51:42,856
Is he the one?

665
00:51:44,790 --> 00:51:45,831
I'm not completely sure.

666
00:51:46,023 --> 00:51:47,555
As I mentioned,

667
00:51:47,556 --> 00:51:48,790
he was wearing a mask.

668
00:51:49,689 --> 00:51:50,401
What about the voice?

669
00:51:50,402 --> 00:51:52,856
It sounds similar, I guess...

670
00:51:54,023 --> 00:51:54,956
Really?

671
00:51:58,056 --> 00:52:00,055
That's right, yes.

672
00:52:00,056 --> 00:52:02,256
I think it could be him...

673
00:52:03,523 --> 00:52:04,389
Okay.

674
00:52:04,390 --> 00:52:06,622
I'll make him put on a mask,
so take another look.

675
00:52:06,623 --> 00:52:07,390
Sure.

676
00:52:09,590 --> 00:52:10,423
Put this on.

677
00:52:12,490 --> 00:52:14,056
Put this on and look in the mirror.

678
00:52:17,156 --> 00:52:18,092
Hurry up.

679
00:52:18,823 --> 00:52:20,756
Do we really have
to go through all this?

680
00:52:21,696 --> 00:52:22,830
Just put it on.

681
00:52:30,890 --> 00:52:31,990
Gosh.

682
00:52:38,156 --> 00:52:40,610
Koh Ju-ran! Come out of there!

683
00:52:41,723 --> 00:52:42,923
Jeez.

684
00:52:46,223 --> 00:52:47,355
Hey,

685
00:52:47,356 --> 00:52:48,990
so this is just a feeling, right?

686
00:52:49,756 --> 00:52:51,455
We have a witness here too.

687
00:52:51,456 --> 00:52:53,090
Are you seriously...

688
00:53:11,423 --> 00:53:13,223
Are you really sure
he's the one who kidnapped me?

689
00:53:14,256 --> 00:53:16,023
Are you sure he's the one?

690
00:53:16,823 --> 00:53:18,389
I mean, back then,

691
00:53:18,390 --> 00:53:20,556
he was wearing a mask, so I couldn't...

692
00:53:20,990 --> 00:53:21,989
No, no.

693
00:53:21,990 --> 00:53:24,223
Ms. Jeon, you don't have to ask.
It's ridiculous.

694
00:53:24,523 --> 00:53:27,289
We have Mr. Gi's wife as an alibi
that proves everything, right?

695
00:53:27,290 --> 00:53:29,255
Then that's it, right?

696
00:53:29,256 --> 00:53:31,722
Or does that mean that Mr. Gi

697
00:53:31,723 --> 00:53:33,523
and the wife are co-conspirators?

698
00:53:34,473 --> 00:53:36,955
I was half asleep,
but my husband came in,

699
00:53:36,956 --> 00:53:38,190
and we held hands too.

700
00:53:38,856 --> 00:53:40,623
The time isn't exact,

701
00:53:40,890 --> 00:53:42,455
but was it around midnight?

702
00:53:42,456 --> 00:53:44,156
- I think that's about right.
- Oh.

703
00:53:44,590 --> 00:53:46,289
What time was it again?

704
00:53:46,290 --> 00:53:48,590
It was a little past 1 AM.

705
00:53:50,790 --> 00:53:53,290
Hey,
stop before this gets any bigger.

706
00:53:54,476 --> 00:53:55,843
Can I at least
put the mask on him?

707
00:53:56,423 --> 00:53:57,922
You're pushing it...

708
00:53:57,923 --> 00:54:00,523
Please let me know
when you put on the mask.

709
00:54:01,223 --> 00:54:03,023
This is about a family's life here.

710
00:54:13,923 --> 00:54:15,322
Mr. Gi Su-jong,

711
00:54:15,323 --> 00:54:16,556
please put on the mask.

712
00:54:19,856 --> 00:54:21,123
Put on the mask.

713
00:54:21,890 --> 00:54:23,790
Okay, I'll do it.

714
00:54:30,956 --> 00:54:32,156
Please stand
in front of the mirror.

715
00:54:51,723 --> 00:54:52,723
It's kind of vague.

716
00:54:58,823 --> 00:55:00,556
Is my wife here too?

717
00:55:02,390 --> 00:55:03,722
Seon,

718
00:55:03,723 --> 00:55:04,756
are you here?

719
00:55:05,556 --> 00:55:06,522
No way.

720
00:55:06,523 --> 00:55:07,990
He was with his wife.

721
00:55:08,790 --> 00:55:09,823
That can't be.

722
00:55:13,890 --> 00:55:14,906
No.

723
00:55:15,290 --> 00:55:17,603
I don't think he's the one.

724
00:55:44,056 --> 00:55:45,050
Hold on.

725
00:55:46,709 --> 00:55:47,776
What now?

726
00:55:48,356 --> 00:55:49,690
When Gyun had that accident,

727
00:55:50,423 --> 00:55:51,523
you were there, right?

728
00:55:57,223 --> 00:55:58,189
Honey, let's go.

729
00:55:58,869 --> 00:55:59,869
Okay.

730
00:56:13,123 --> 00:56:15,355
I'm sorry, Su-jong.

731
00:56:15,356 --> 00:56:17,289
I didn't mean to drag Hwal-sung into this.

732
00:56:17,290 --> 00:56:19,489
No, it's okay. Don't say that.

733
00:56:19,490 --> 00:56:22,589
What if I hadn't known
you came in late?

734
00:56:22,590 --> 00:56:24,290
You might be in jail right now.

735
00:56:25,823 --> 00:56:27,390
Seon saved Su-jong.

736
00:56:27,622 --> 00:56:29,666
You really married well, Su-jong.

737
00:56:30,923 --> 00:56:33,122
Oh, Yi-gyeong,
thank you so much for today.

738
00:56:33,123 --> 00:56:34,422
You're not feeling well too.

739
00:56:34,423 --> 00:56:35,490
It's nothing.

740
00:56:39,656 --> 00:56:42,022
Seon,
I'm going to take a little nap.

741
00:56:42,023 --> 00:56:43,790
Oh, go ahead. You must be tired.

742
00:56:59,923 --> 00:57:02,303
I thought you were
cheating on me, but I guess not.

743
00:57:02,723 --> 00:57:04,423
Hey, that's nonsense.

744
00:57:06,770 --> 00:57:08,822
You need to disinfect this
and change the bandage.

745
00:57:08,823 --> 00:57:09,756
It might get infected.

746
00:57:10,449 --> 00:57:12,171
I'll do it when I get home later.

747
00:57:14,169 --> 00:57:15,136
What about your phone?

748
00:57:15,490 --> 00:57:16,423
Oh.

749
00:57:17,823 --> 00:57:18,690
It ended up like this.

750
00:57:20,756 --> 00:57:22,990
Hurry and get a new one.
I get anxious if I can't reach you.

751
00:57:23,523 --> 00:57:24,490
Okay.

752
00:57:28,776 --> 00:57:30,976
Your hair is a mess too.
You should get a haircut.

753
00:57:34,923 --> 00:57:36,523
It was you who kidnapped her, right?

754
00:57:46,963 --> 00:57:48,363
You'll explain it to me, right?

755
00:57:55,596 --> 00:57:56,462
Yes.

756
00:57:58,656 --> 00:57:59,455
Okay.

757
00:57:59,456 --> 00:58:00,856
- Let's eat.
- Okay.

758
00:58:51,556 --> 00:58:52,622
Hello?

759
00:58:52,623 --> 00:58:53,790
Ms. Kim Seon.

760
00:58:56,723 --> 00:58:57,718
Yes?

761
00:58:58,336 --> 00:59:00,336
It's going as planned, right?

762
00:59:06,823 --> 00:59:07,790
Right?

763
00:59:49,723 --> 00:59:50,789
I'VE BEEN STRANGE LATELY, HAVEN'T I?

764
00:59:50,790 --> 00:59:52,623
AND YOU'RE PROBABLY RESENTING ME A LOT

765
01:00:10,690 --> 01:00:13,623
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

766
01:00:13,923 --> 01:00:14,989
Let's sell this building.

767
01:00:14,990 --> 01:00:15,890
Why suddenly?

768
01:00:15,891 --> 01:00:18,251
Sell this building to that Real Capital
or whatever they are.

769
01:00:18,490 --> 01:00:20,255
Three billion. Sounds good, right?

770
01:00:20,256 --> 01:00:23,122
I'll give you some time to think about it.

771
01:00:23,123 --> 01:00:26,522
They're building
the largest building in Asia here.

772
01:00:26,523 --> 01:00:29,189
So Hwal-sung know that
the Seyoon Building

773
01:00:29,190 --> 01:00:30,689
was included in the redevelopment??

774
01:00:30,690 --> 01:00:31,722
Are we really friends?

775
01:00:31,723 --> 01:00:33,289
What do you think of me as?

776
01:00:33,290 --> 01:00:34,889
It seems like there's an issue.

777
01:00:34,890 --> 01:00:36,753
Please wait a bit longer.

778
01:00:37,056 --> 01:00:39,255
Hee-ju, how do you do it?

779
01:00:39,256 --> 01:00:40,255
Do what?

780
01:00:40,256 --> 01:00:41,356
Riding the line?

781
01:00:42,397 --> 01:00:44,002
Why are you deciding that?

782
01:00:44,003 --> 01:00:45,655
I think it should be 30 billion.

783
01:00:46,956 --> 01:00:48,555
Oh, this is fun.

784
01:00:48,556 --> 01:00:50,255
But I did mention last time

785
01:00:50,256 --> 01:00:52,690
that this is the last chance
to quietly move on?

